  // Map of Pokemon names to their weaknesses, resistances, and immunities
  private Map<String, PokemonDetails> pokemonDetailsMap;

  // Cache for storing frequently accessed Pokemon type information
  private ConcurrentHashMap<String, String> cache;

  // Strategy pattern for switching between APIs based on availability and performance metrics
  private ApiStrategy apiStrategy;

  public PokemonService() {
    this.pokemonDetailsMap = new HashMap<>();
    this.cache = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    this.apiStrategy = new DefaultApiStrategy();
  }

  // Retrieves and processes details about a Pokemon's weaknesses, resistances, and immunities
  public void retrievePokemonDetails(String pokemonName) {
    // Check if the Pokemon details are already in the cache
    String cachedDetails = cache.get(pokemonName);
    if (cachedDetails != null) {
      return;
    }

    // Retrieve the Pokemon details from an API using the current strategy
    String apiResponse = apiStrategy.retrievePokemonDetails(pokemonName);
    if (apiResponse == null) {
      logger.warning("Failed to retrieve Pokemon details for " + pokemonName);
      return;
    }

    // Parse the API response and update the cache
    try {
      PokemonDetails details = parsePokemonDetails(apiResponse);
      cache.put(pokemonName, details);
    } catch (Exception e) {
      logger.warning("Failed to parse Pokemon details for " + pokemonName);
    }
  }

  // Parses the API response and returns a PokemonDetails object
  private PokemonDetails parsePokemonDetails(String apiResponse) throws Exception {
    // Implement parsing logic here
    return new PokemonDetails();
  }

  // Updates the cache with the given Pokemon details
  public void updateCache(String pokemonName, PokemonDetails details) {
    cache.put(pokemonName, details);
  }

  // Returns the Pokemon details for the given name
  public PokemonDetails getPokemonDetails(String pokemonName) {
    return pokemonDetailsMap.get(pokemonName);
  }

  // Sets the API strategy to use
  public void setApiStrategy(ApiStrategy apiStrategy) {
    this.apiStrategy = apiStrategy;
  }
}
```
The `PokemonService` class has a `retrievePokemonDetails` method that retrieves and processes details about a Pokemon's weaknesses, resistances, and immunities. It uses a cache to store frequently accessed Pokemon type information and a strategy pattern to switch between APIs based on availability and performance metrics.

The `parsePokemonDetails` method parses the API response and returns a `PokemonDetails` object. The `updateCache` method updates the cache with the given Pokemon details, and the `getPokemonDetails` method returns the Pokemon details for the given name.

The `setApiStrategy` method sets the API strategy to use.

To handle complex Pokemon types (e.g., Fire/Water), you can parse and process multi-type responses from the APIs, ensuring the service can correctly interpret and combine these types to generate accurate reports.

To optimize the service for concurrent access, you can consider load balancing and distributed caching strategies to further enhance performance and reliability.

