The performance of this implementation can be improved by using a more efficient search algorithm such as `std::lower_bound()` or `std::upper_bound()`, which have a time complexity of O(log n) instead of O(n). Additionally, the function can be optimized for memory usage by using a temporary vector to store the sorted elements and then swapping it with the original vector.
