<?php

class UserAccountManager {
    private $db;

    public function __construct(Database $db) {
        $this->db = $db;
    }

    public function handleRequest() {
        $request = $_POST;

        // Validate request data
        if (!$this->validateRequest($request)) {
            return $this->errorResponse('Invalid request data');
        }

        // Handle sub-action
        switch ($request['sub_action']) {
            case 'create':
                return $this->createUser($request);
            case 'update':
                return $this->updateUser($request);
            case 'delete':
                return $this->deleteUser($request);
            case 'retrieve':
                return $this->getUser($request);
        }
    }

    private function validateRequest(array $request) {
        // Check for required fields
        if (!isset($request['name']) || !isset($request['email']) || !isset($request['password'])) {
            return false;
        }

        // Validate email format
        if (!filter_var($request['email'], FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL)) {
            return false;
        }

        // Validate password length
        if (strlen($request['password']) < 8) {
            return false;
        }

        // Validate name length
        if (strlen($request['name']) < 2) {
            return false;
        }

        return true;
    }

    private function createUser(array $request) {
        try {
            // Generate unique username based on name field
            $username = $this->generateUniqueUsername($request['name']);

            // Save user to database
            $user = new User();
            $user->setName($request['name']);
            $user->setEmail($request['email']);
            $user->setPassword($request['password']);
            $user->setUsername($username);
            $this->db->save($user);

            // Return success response
            return $this->successResponse('User created successfully');
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            // Handle exception and return error response
            return $this->errorResponse('Error creating user: ' . $e->getMessage());
        }
    }

    private function updateUser(array $request) {
        try {
            // Check if id exists in database
            $user = $this->db->getById($request['id']);
            if (!$user) {
                return $this->errorResponse('Invalid user ID');
            }

            // Update user data
            $user->setName($request['name']);
            $user->setEmail($request['email']);
            $user->setPassword($request['password']);
            $this->db->save($user);

            // Return success response
            return $this->successResponse('User updated successfully');
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            // Handle exception and return error response
            return $this->errorResponse('Error updating user: ' . $e->getMessage());
        }
    }

    private function deleteUser(array $request) {
        try {
            // Check if id exists in database
            $user = $this->db->getById($request['id']);
            if (!$user) {
                return $this->errorResponse('Invalid user ID');
            }

            // Delete user from database
            $this->db->delete($user);

            // Return success response
            return $this->successResponse('User deleted successfully');
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            // Handle exception and return error response
            return $this->errorResponse('Error deleting user: ' . $e->getMessage());
        }
    }

    private function getUser(array $request) {
        try {
            // Check if id exists in database
            $user = $this->db->getById($request['id']);
            if (!$user) {
                return $this->errorResponse('Invalid user ID');
            }

            // Return full user profile
            return $this->successResponse('User retrieved successfully', $user);
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            // Handle exception and return error response
            return $this->errorResponse('Error retrieving user: ' . $e->getMessage());
        }
    }

    private function generateUniqueUsername(string $name) {
        // Generate unique username based on name field
        $username = strtolower($name);
        $i = 1;
        while ($this->db->getByUsername($username)) {
            $username = $name . '-' . $i++;
        }
        return $username;
    }

    private function successResponse(string $message, $data = null) {
        // Return JSON response with 'success' message and data
        return json_encode([
            'message' => 'success',
            'data' => $data
        ]);
    }

    private function errorResponse(string $message) {
        // Return JSON response with 'error' message and details
        return json_encode([
            'message' => 'error',
            'details' => $message
        ]);
    }
}
```
This code defines a `UserAccountManager` class that handles user requests for creating, updating, deleting, or retrieving user accounts. The class uses a `Database` object to interact with the database and validate user data. It also includes methods for generating unique usernames based on the name field and handling exceptions and errors gracefully.

The `handleRequest()` method is the main entry point of the class and takes care of validating the request data, handling sub-actions, and returning appropriate responses. The `validateRequest()` method checks if all required fields are present in the request data and validates email format and password length. The `createUser()`, `updateUser()`, `deleteUser()`, and `getUser()` methods handle specific actions based on the 'sub_action' field of the request data. They also include error handling to prevent system bottlenecks or data corruption.

The `generateUniqueUsername()` method generates a unique username based on the name field by checking if it already exists in the database and incrementing the suffix until a unique value is found. The `successResponse()` and `errorResponse()` methods return JSON responses with 'message' and 'data' fields, respectively.

This code should be optimized for performance under heavy load, managing potential race conditions during concurrent updates. It should also ensure efficient resource usage and robust error handling to prevent system bottlenecks or data corruption."]

