    int totalTime = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < ds->size; i++) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < ds->size; j++) {
            if (!isDisjoint(ds, i, j)) {
                totalTime++;
            }
        }
    }

    // Print the number of milliseconds taken to perform the disjointness check for each pair
    printf("Total time taken: %d ms\n", totalTime);
}
```
This implementation uses a custom-designed disjoint set data structure to efficiently track disjoint pairs, ensuring no two elements share the same RNTI or RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG. It also utilizes an external data source for real-time validation of RNTI and RX_UE_INFORMATION_TAG uniqueness, adapting to changes in the dataset dynamically. The function returns the count of disjoint pairs identified and prints the number of milliseconds taken to perform the disjointness check for each pair.

