The code also includes a caching mechanism for storing real-time terrain data in memory, which can be used to improve performance by reducing the number of requests made to the external map service API. The caching mechanism is implemented using a dictionary that stores terrain data for each region.

To update camera speed based on user interactions, the code uses a `while` loop that continuously checks the current region and updates the camera speed accordingly. The updated camera speed is then stored in the real-time terrain data cache for the current region.

The code also includes error handling and logging to capture performance metrics and errors, as well as a testing strategy to validate performance under various conditions.']

