The `populate_pdcp_pdu_list` function is thread-safe, meaning that it can handle concurrent access and modification of the data structure without race conditions. This is achieved by using a mutex to protect the hash table when adding PDUs and SPS values.

The `populate_pdcp_pdu_list_threadsafe` function is similar to `populate_pdcp_pdu_list`, but it uses a different approach to handle concurrent access and modification of the data structure. In this function, a mutex is used to protect the hash table when adding PDUs and SPS values, but the mutex is only locked for a short period of time while checking if the current PDU or SPS value is already present in the hash table. This approach can be more efficient than the previous one, as it reduces the overhead of locking and unlocking the mutex multiple times.

The `populate_pdcp_pdu_list` function also provides a fallback mechanism for handling high-load conditions. If the population process encounters excessive collisions or other performance bottlenecks, it can gracefully degrade by reducing the number of PDUs to be processed and providing reasonable fallback mechanisms in case of excessive collisions or other performance bottlenecks.

