            LTE_RRC_NAS_Transaction_T *transaction = transactions[i];
            pthread_mutex_unlock(&transaction_lock);
            return transaction;
        }
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&transaction_lock);
    return NULL;
}

// Free the dynamic array and lock when no longer needed
void free_transactions() {
    for (size_t i = 0; i < num_transactions; i++) {
        free(transactions[i]);
    }
    free(transactions);
    pthread_mutex_destroy(&transaction_lock);
}
```
This code defines a structure `LTE_RRC_NAS_Transaction` to represent a transaction, and a dynamic array of pointers to store the transactions. The `init_transactions()` function initializes the dynamic array and locks it for thread-safe access. The `add_transaction()` function adds a new transaction to the end of the dynamic array, while the `get_transaction()` function retrieves a transaction by its ID. Finally, the `free_transactions()` function frees the dynamic array and lock when no longer needed.

This implementation uses a mutex to ensure thread-safe access to the dynamic array, and it also handles potential race conditions and memory leaks. The system can handle high transaction volumes without degradation in performance by using a fixed size for the dynamic array and avoiding unnecessary reallocations. Additionally, the system is designed to be easy to integrate with existing components and future scalability, balancing the trade-offs between efficiency, usability, and maintainability.']

